msgid "Cross-compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:13
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:15
msgid ""
"Open Robotics provides pre-built ROS 2 packages for multiple platforms, but "
"a number of developers still rely on `cross-compilation <https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_compiler>`__ for different reasons such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:16
msgid "The development machine does not match the target system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:17
msgid ""
"Tuning the build for specific core architecture (e.g. setting -mcpu=cortex-"
"a53 -mfpu=neon-fp-armv8 when building for Raspberry Pi3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Targeting a file system other than the ones supported by the pre-built "
"images released by Open Robotics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:21
msgid "How does it work ?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:23
msgid ""
"Cross-compiling simple software (e.g. no dependencies on external libraries) "
"is relatively simple and only requiring a cross-compiler toolchain to be "
"used instead of the native toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:25
msgid "There are a number of factors which make this process more complex:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:26
msgid ""
"The software being built must support the target architecture. Architecture "
"specific code must be properly isolated and enabled during the build "
"according to the target architecture. Examples include assembly code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:29
msgid ""
"All dependencies (e.g. libraries) must be present, either as pre-built or "
"cross-compiled packages, before the target software using them is cross-"
"compiled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:30
msgid ""
"When building software stacks (as opposed to standalone software) using "
"build tools (e.g. colcon), it is expected that the build tool provides a "
"mechanism to allow the developer to enable cross-compilation on the "
"underlying build system used by each piece of software in the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:33
msgid "Alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/About-Cross-Compilation.rst:35
msgid ""
"An alternative to cross-compilation is to `build multi-platform Docker "
"images <https://github.com/docker/buildx#building-multi-platform-images>`__ "
"using ``docker buildx``."
msgstr ""
